process-other-module.m on the machine's GPU: its GPU process and its target
region call another module's procedures, which the device compiles copied
from that module's merk bytecode. The processes' kernel takes half of the
GPU's units (MERK_GPU_PROCESS_UNITS), so that the region has the rest.
Nothing is left over.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch -I %S/Inputs %libomp-flags %S/Inputs/device_helpers.m %S/process-other-module.m -o %t
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_GPU_PROCESS_UNITS=50 OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY MERK_CHECK_MESSAGES=1 MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 timeout -k 1 60 %t gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %S/process-other-module.m --check-prefixes=CHECK,FREED --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
